@startuml donor-first-deployment
!theme plain
title Remote worker on a donor machine, first deployment: one invitation, one command; the private key stays in the keyring; the posture is locked by the donor (the machine's owner)

actor "Donor (the machine's owner)" as ADM
participant "curator remote-worker init\n(donor install)" as C
participant "Privileged helper\n(sudoers: this binary only)" as PH
participant "Harness OS user\nswarma-rw-<project>" as U
database "OS keyring\n(of the harness user)" as KR
database "DNS (DNSSEC)\nTXT _swarma, SSHFP, TLSA" as DNS
participant "Join point\n(our host, HTTPS, two verbs)" as JP
actor "Operator (our side)\nor orchestrator with onboard grant" as OP
participant "Trust registry + key keeper\n(our host)" as T

== 1. invitation ==
OP -> ADM: invitation {join point, root fingerprint, one-time code,\nproject, role, expires} over a second channel

== 2. local provisioning ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker init <invitation>
C -> DNS: resolve join point; require DNSSEC-validated TXT (root fingerprint), SSHFP, TLSA
alt DNS unsigned or fingerprint differs from the invitation
  C --> ADM: refused{dns_fingerprint_mismatch}
else anchors agree
  C -> PH: create user, home 0700, pf/nftables rules by UID,\nsandbox profile, quotas, launchd/systemd unit
  PH --> C: uid
  C -> KR: generate key pair inside the keyring (never exported)
  C -> C: self-signed certificate {pubkey, name, role, contact, expires}\nsigned over the invitation code; show fingerprint to ADM
end

== 3. join ==
C -> JP: POST cert (TLS pinned by TLSA / invitation)
JP -> OP: new certificate for invitation <code>: fingerprint F
OP -> ADM: read back F over the second channel
alt F differs
  OP -> JP: reject
  JP --> C: refused
else F matches
  OP -> T: pin key as external identity; root signs admission "K admitted with role R";\ngrants: post to worker thread, read own mailbox, no delegation, expiry
  OP -> OP: credential package {our root pubkey, host, SSH host key fingerprint,\nworkplace user, binding digest, pinned harness release, expiry}\nencrypted to K (X25519 + AEAD), signed by the operator
  OP -> JP: package ready for <code>
  C -> JP: collect (signed by K)
  JP --> C: package
  C -> KR: decrypt inside the keyring boundary
  C -> C: verify operator signature against the root fingerprint (DNS + invitation);\nwrite LOCKED machine config: tool_posture=lockdown, permissions=remote-auto,\nmcp_package_allowlist=[swarma-remote-tools], passable_env_names=[], binding, pinned release;\ninstall the remote-tools declaration into profile remote-worker
  C --> ADM: registered; waiting for tasks (status, stop, revoke available)
end

== 4. workplace on our host ==
OP -> T: provision workplace for K (dispatcher, grant user.create):\nOS user, authorized_keys = K with restrict + forced command swarma-rb-exec, firewall by UID
note right of T: see remote-worker-turn for the connection
@enduml
